NAME
    which - identify how command names resolve

SYNOPSIS
    which <name>...

DESCRIPTION
    For each <name> (matched case-insensitively), prints a line stating
    how the shell resolves it:

    <name>: shell builtin       Language keyword/builtin or shell
                                builtin not overridden by the host.
    <name>: alias for <target>  Built-in or module alias.
    <name>: command             Module command, host command, or
                                shipped program.
    which: no <name>            No matching command found.

EXAMPLES
    which cd grep quit
    which nosuch || echo missing

EXIT STATUS
    0   Every named command resolved.
    1   Missing arguments, or at least one name did not resolve.

SEE ALSO
    command(1), help(1), man(1)
